dit suite: 83 passed, four diagnostic ignores. Final frozen NUC binary passed all 735 uncached and all 735 cached differential conformance comparisons across interpreter, baseline and LLVM (1,470 total). Compiler lib and TS all-target Clippy passed with warnings denied; Python/Lua LLVM library checks passed. Existing attribute-derive-macro future-incompatibility warning is unchanged.\n\nFresh-process Rust allocation audit, same source fixtures, local diagnostic binary (not timings): tiny uncached/store/hit 2351/3671/1831 allocation requests, 653700/790841/450825 requested bytes; wide uncached/store/hit 75758/77233/1835 requests, 22175041/23623372/730633 bytes. Reports /private/tmp/ts-small-allocations-process.json. Native-library/libc/slab allocations are excluded and requested bytes are not RSS. These counts confirm the preceding selective cache work avoids most frontend allocations; they are not a before/after attribution to lazy LLVM TargetMachine creation.\n\nA linker-only RELR experiment suggested a further ~0.2 ms in some startup controls but adds GLIBC_ABI_DT_RELR to required ABI. Compatibility and ELF static-constructor/relocation work is tracked separately in 45561efaf054a351e041ca53bf386f0b9365808d407cbebc3e1af60a38621df4. No repository linker policy was changed. The profiling task and deferred-target change are complete; the broad native module and compatibility issues remain open. Python/Lua source project caches are not wired by this change and have not been benchmarked here.","files":null}]}